From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Open Arc Authors <dev@openarc.invalid>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 05:01:30 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] openarc: embedder: built-in ad blocking

Plan C16. Ad blocking on Chromium's own subresource filter
(//components/subresource_filter), the engine behind Chrome's Better Ads
enforcement, without the Chrome Web Store, extensions or Google's ruleset
component:

- openarc/browser/openarc_ad_blocker.{h,mm}: AdBlocker hands the
  EasyList + EasyPrivacy ruleset (converted at build time with
  ruleset_converter and shipped in the framework's Resources/AdBlock, see
  chromium-bridge/build-adblock-ruleset.sh in the Open Arc repository) to
  Chrome's RulesetService, which indexes it once per version and publishes
  it to every renderer. --openarc-ad-block-ruleset=<dir> loads another
  ruleset directory (the entry point of the planned updater, TODO in the
  header). The global switch is the Local State pref
  openarc.ad_blocking.enabled (default on); the per-site allow list is
  Chrome's ADS content setting.
- AdBlockTabHelper, attached with Chrome's tab helpers: forces the
  filter's activation (DevtoolsInteractionTracker, the switch DevTools'
  Page.setAdBlockingEnabled uses) from the global switch before every
  main-frame navigation, since Chrome only activates it on pages Safe
  Browsing lists, and counts the loads it blocked on the current page from
  the filter's console messages.
- OpenArcBrowserMainExtraParts registers the pref and loads the ruleset
  (PostBrowserStart).
- Bridge: OACApplication.adBlockingEnabled / adBlockingRulesetVersion,
  OACSiteSettings (first implementation: ad blocking and zoom; the other
  settings stay no-ops until C12), -setAdBlockingEnabled:forOrigin: /
  -isAdBlockingEnabledForOrigin:, OACTab.blockedAdCount.

Without it, the subresource filter stays in Chrome's dry-run/ad-tagging
mode and blocks nothing (Safe Browsing is off in Open Arc).
